      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm doing a quick audit on a new fintech app we're building. Can you give me a checklist of the main WCAG 2.1 requirements I should look for regarding color contrast and screen reader compatibility?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! For color contrast, ensure text and background colors have a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text to meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards. Ensure that interactive elements have adequate contrast ratios as well.\n\nFor screen reader compatibility, make sure all mean_id elements, like images and logos, have appropriate alt text. Check that all functionality is keyboard-accessible, including forms and dynamic content. Content should be structured with proper ARIA landmark roles and properties so that screen readers can accurately interpret the page layout. Also, ensure that captions or transcripts are available for any multimedia that needs it.",
